        prompts: {
          human: "Mauscheln (also known as 'Maus' or 'Lurk') is a traditional German gambling and trick-taking game popular in the 19th and early 20th centuries. Similar to games in the 'Rams' family, it focuses on the choice to either 'Sneak' (Mauscheln)—committing to win at least two tricks—or 'Pass' to avoid a penalty. It is famous for its fast rounds, rapidly escalating pots, and the high-stakes risk of the 'Bête' (a penalty equal to the entire pot).",
